From 4095cebe3e214f57536cdb1415ca6a81694a4dd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Eden (Doris) build" <doris@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:57:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] turnip (Doris): GMEM must be 15% faster to win; timing
 without per-pass trace copies; count reinterpreting views

- autotune (profiled): pick GMEM for a pass only when it is at least 15% faster. The CCU switch
  between SYSMEM and GMEM (flush, invalidate, wait for idle) is paid outside the timed pass, before
  the next SYSMEM pass, so small GMEM wins (5-17% in TotK on Eden) can cost more than they save.
- Report: leave out the tracepoints recorded inside render passes (clears, GMEM loads/stores,
  resolves): copying them into the command buffer's trace adds a wait-for-idle per pass, which
  inflated the per-pass overhead the last report showed. Figures are now labelled per second.
- Report: count views of Eden's mutable color images in another format (same or other UBWC
  compression type, RGBA/BGRA swapped), to see whether TotK reinterprets its images at all; that
  decides whether UBWC can be turned on for them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014Ps8wnhVXtSU7d88gGtyHX
